{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt"],"declarations":113,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.squaredToLinearTransition_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.squaredToLinearTransition_refl","kind":"instance","line":1171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1171-L1173","doc":"Reflexivity instance for `SquaredToLinearTransition`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition.exponent_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition.exponent_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1169-L1169","doc":"Effective exponent agreement at level `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1166-L1166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SquaredToLinearTransition","kind":"class","line":1158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1158-L1169","doc":"**Squared-to-linear transition — typeclass.**\nHeuristic effective-exponent description: per-`(k, α_k)`,\nthe level-k branching fraction is approximately\n`d_q(μ)^{α_k} / Σ d_q(ν)^{α_k}`, with α_k → 1 as k → ∞.\nThe rigorous statement is the O(1/(k-3)) `ConvergenceBound`\ntypeclass above; this class records the heuristic exponent at\na chosen `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingAtK3_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingAtK3_refl","kind":"instance","line":1139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1139-L1143","doc":"Reflexivity instance: when both arguments are the same value,\nthe class is trivially inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3.equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3.equal","kind":"theorem","line":1137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1137-L1137","doc":"f^{(3)}_μ = W_μ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1135-L1135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.BranchingAtK3","kind":"class","line":1130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1130-L1137","doc":"**Branching at k=3 — typeclass alias.**\nThe level-3 branching fraction equals the Wedderburn weight\n`W_μ = d_q(μ)² / [3]_q!`. The substantive equality is proved\nin `ConfinedKnotBinding.lean §8`; this class records the link\nper-`μ` so callers can bind the proved instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cumulativeErrorHarmonic_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cumulativeErrorHarmonic_zero","kind":"instance","line":1119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1119-L1126","doc":"**Zero-error (reflexivity)**: when `cumError = 0`, the bound\nholds with LHS = 0 (assuming the RHS is non-negative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic.bound","kind":"theorem","line":1117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1117-L1117","doc":"`|cumError| ≤ H_{K-3} · C_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1114-L1114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.CumulativeErrorHarmonic","kind":"class","line":1107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1107-L1117","doc":"**Cumulative-error harmonic bound — typeclass.**\nPer-`(K, C_q)` witness that the cumulative error from levels\n4 to K is bounded by `H_{K-3} · C_q`, where `H_n` is the\n`n`-th harmonic number. The full proof reduces to summing the\n`O(1/(k-3))` per-level bound; the harmonic bound is the\nclosed-form result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.knotInvariantConvergence_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.knotInvariantConvergence_refl","kind":"instance","line":1079,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1079-L1089","doc":"**Self-convergence (reflexivity)**: when `a_k = a_inf`, the\nbound holds with LHS = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.knotInvariantConvergence_of_fact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.knotInvariantConvergence_of_fact","kind":"instance","line":1072,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1072-L1077","doc":"**Default instance from a `Fact` witness on the rate bound**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence.bound","kind":"theorem","line":1070,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1070-L1070","doc":"Knot-invariant level-k → ∞ rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1067,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1067-L1067","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.KnotInvariantConvergence","kind":"class","line":1060,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1060-L1070","doc":"**Knot-invariant convergence — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nPer-instance witness for the rate at which the level-k knot\ninvariant approaches its limit. Like `ConvergenceBound`, the\nfree-real form has no a-priori link; the bound is propagated\nfrom `convergence_bound` via the linear-combination definition\nof `a_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.convergence_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.convergence_bound","kind":"theorem","line":1036,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1036-L1041","doc":"Per-instance form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.convergenceBound_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.convergenceBound_refl","kind":"instance","line":1025,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1025-L1034","doc":"**Self-convergence (reflexivity)**: when `f_k = f_inf`, the\nbound holds with LHS = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound.bound","kind":"theorem","line":1023,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1023-L1023","doc":"The Kerov–Vershik O(1/(k-3)) bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1020,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1020-L1020","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.ConvergenceBound","kind":"class","line":1014,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L1014-L1023","doc":"**q-Plancherel convergence — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nThe free-real bound `|f_k - f_inf| ≤ C_q / (k-3)` has no\na-priori semantic link to the actual branching fractions. Per\ninstance, the caller witnesses the bound for the specific\n`(k, C_q, f_k, f_inf)` they use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingFraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingFraction","kind":"def","line":972,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L972-L986","doc":"The Wedderburn-weighted branching fraction at level k.\n\nf_μ^{(k)} = Σ_{lam ⊢ k} w_lam × m_μ^lam / Σ_{lam ⊢ k} w_lam × Σ_ν m_ν^lam\n\nwhere w_lam = d_q(lam)² / [k]_q! is the Wedderburn weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branch_31_to_111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branch_31_to_111","kind":"theorem","line":965,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L965-L968","doc":"`(3,1) ⊢ 4 → (1,1,1) ⊢ 3`: not contained, so the multiplicity is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_31_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_31_21","kind":"theorem","line":962,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L962-L963","doc":"`(3,1) ⊢ 4 → (2,1) ⊢ 3`: the skew shape is the single cell `(0,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_31_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_31_3","kind":"theorem","line":959,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L959-L960","doc":"`(3,1) ⊢ 4 → (3) ⊢ 3`: the skew shape is the single cell `(1,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p111","kind":"def","line":956,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L956-L957","doc":"`(1,1,1) ⊢ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p21","kind":"def","line":954,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L954-L955","doc":"`(2,1) ⊢ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p3","kind":"def","line":952,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L952-L953","doc":"`(3) ⊢ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.p31","kind":"def","line":950,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L950-L951","doc":"`(3,1) ⊢ 4`, the source of the branching row below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_1111_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_1111_check","kind":"theorem","line":910,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L910-L910","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_4_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_4_check","kind":"theorem","line":909,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L909-L909","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_211_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_211_check","kind":"theorem","line":908,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L908-L908","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_22_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_22_check","kind":"theorem","line":907,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L907-L907","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_31_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_31_check","kind":"theorem","line":893,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L893-L906","doc":"Branching table H₄ → H₃ (verified by SYT enumeration):\n\n| lam ⊢ 4     | m_{(3)} | m_{(2,1)} | m_{(1,1,1)} |\n|------------|---------|-----------|-------------|\n| (4)        | 1       | 0         | 0           |\n| (3,1)      | 1       | 1         | 0           |\n| (2,2)      | 0       | 1         | 0           |\n| (2,1,1)    | 0       | 1         | 1           |\n| (1,1,1,1)  | 0       | 0         | 1           |\n\nTotal: Σ m = (2, 3, 2) → dim-weighted: 2×1 + 3×2 + 2×1 = 10\nAnd dim((3,1)) = 3, dim((2,2)) = 2, etc.\nCheck: Σ_μ m_μ^{(3,1)} × dim(μ) = 1×1 + 1×2 = 3 = dim((3,1)) ✓ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitions3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitions3","kind":"def","line":889,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L889-L891","doc":"The three partitions of 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitions4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitions4","kind":"def","line":885,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L885-L887","doc":"The five partitions of 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.qBranchingCorrection_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.qBranchingCorrection_refl","kind":"instance","line":874,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L874-L881","doc":"**Self-correction (reflexivity)**: when `qDim = classicalDim`,\nthe bound holds with LHS = 0 (RHS non-negative when `h_sq ≥ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection.bound","kind":"theorem","line":872,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L872-L872","doc":"Per-cell `O(h²)` perturbation bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":869,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L869-L869","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.QBranchingCorrection","kind":"class","line":864,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L864-L872","doc":"**q-branching correction — typeclass.**\nPer-`(lam, k)` witness that the q-deformed branching dimension\ndiffers from the classical one by `O(h²)` per skew cell,\nwhere `h = q - q⁻¹`. Full proof pending d_q formalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.fominBranchingIdentity_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.fominBranchingIdentity_refl","kind":"instance","line":846,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L846-L848","doc":"Reflexivity instance for `FominBranchingIdentity`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity.identity","kind":"theorem","line":844,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L844-L844","doc":"The sum on the LHS equals the closed-form RHS at `(k, μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":841,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L841-L841","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.FominBranchingIdentity","kind":"class","line":832,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L832-L844","doc":"**Fomin branching identity — typeclass.**\nPer-`(k, μ)` witness that `Σ_{lam ⊢ k} dim(lam) × m_μ^lam\n= (k!/n!) × dim(μ)`, where `n = μ.size`. The full proof\nrequires the RSK bijection (counting pairs of SYT) and a\nMathlib gap on q-Plancherel branching; until that lands,\ncallers supply the identity for the specific `(k, μ)` they\ncare about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_211","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_211","kind":"theorem","line":820,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L820-L821","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_22","kind":"theorem","line":817,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L817-L818","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity_31","kind":"theorem","line":806,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L806-L815","doc":"The branching identity as a concrete check for H₄ → H₃.\n\nFor lam = (3,1), the identity gives:\nm_{(3)}^{(3,1)} × dim(3) + m_{(2,1)}^{(3,1)} × dim(2,1)\n  + m_{(1,1,1)}^{(3,1)} × dim(1,1,1)\n= 1×1 + 1×2 + 0×1 = 3 = dim(3,1).\n\nThis is verified by `decide` without any sorry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classical_dim_identity","kind":"theorem","line":778,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L778-L804","doc":"**Classical branching identity**: for any lam ⊢ k and the branching\nto S_n (n < k):\n\nΣ_{μ ⊢ n} m_μ^lam × dim(μ) = dim(lam)\n\nThis is because restricting V_lam preserves the vector space\ndimension: Res^{S_k}_{S_n}(V_lam) has the same total dimension\nas V_lam.\n\n**Proof structure**:\n1. V_lam is a vector space of dimension dim(lam) = f^lam.\n2. Res^{S_k}_{S_n}(V_lam) decomposes as ⊕_μ V_μ^{m_μ^lam}\n   by Maschke's theorem (S_n semisimple).\n3. dim(Res V_lam) = dim(V_lam) (restriction preserves the\n   underlying vector space).\n4. dim(⊕_μ V_μ^{m_μ}) = Σ_μ m_μ × dim(V_μ).\n5. Therefore: Σ_μ m_μ^lam × dim(μ) = dim(lam). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classicalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.classicalDim","kind":"def","line":773,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L773-L776","doc":"The dimension of V_lam (for S_k at q=1) equals the number of\nSYT of shape lam.  This is the hook-length formula denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.youngCovers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.youngCovers","kind":"def","line":739,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L739-L742","doc":"The covering relation in the Young lattice:\nμ ⋖ lam iff lam = μ + one cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.addCell","kind":"def","line":721,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L721-L737","doc":"Adding a cell to a partition: lam ← c gives a new partition with\none more cell at the chosen position.\n\nThe naive set/append can fail to preserve the weakly-decreasing\ninvariant (e.g. lam = [2,2], row = 1 → [2,3] is unsorted). Sorting\nafter the operation makes `addCell` total without needing an\naddability hypothesis: when the cell *is* addable, sorting is\nthe identity; otherwise sorting moves the incremented part to\nits proper place. The size (sum + 1) is preserved by the sort. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branching_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L715-L717","doc":"Branching multiplicities are non-negative (they're natural numbers). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.branchingMult","kind":"def","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L705-L713","doc":"The branching multiplicity m_μ^lam = f^{lam/μ} = #SYT(lam/μ).\n\nThis counts the number of ways to restrict the H_k representation\nV_lam to H_n, with the μ-component appearing m_μ^lam times.\n\nFor the branching H_k(q) → H_3(q): μ is a partition of 3,\nlam is a partition of k, and m_μ^lam = #SYT(lam/μ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_pos","kind":"theorem","line":658,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L658-L700","doc":"SYT count is positive when lam ⊇ μ (there's always at least one SYT). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L651-L656","doc":"Nonempty skew shape has at least one corner. Backed by\n`PartitionHelpers.skewCorners_nonempty`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_preserves_containment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_preserves_containment","kind":"theorem","line":643,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L643-L649","doc":"Removing the row of a skew cell of lam/μ still leaves a\npartition containing μ. Backed by `PartitionHelpers`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty_axiom","kind":"theorem","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L636-L641","doc":"Skew diagram with more cells in lam than μ has a (lex-maximal)\ncorner. Backed by `PartitionHelpers`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_card_eq_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_card_eq_size","kind":"theorem","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L630-L634","doc":"Partition's Young-diagram cells count equals its size. Backed\nby `PartitionHelpers`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitionHelpers_default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.partitionHelpers_default","kind":"instance","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L619-L628","doc":"**Default `PartitionHelpers` instance** — unconditional: all\nthree fields are proved theorems in this file\n(`Partition.cells_card_eq_size_proved`,\n`skewCorners_nonempty_proved`,\n`removeCorner_preserves_containment_proved`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.removeCorner_preserves_containment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.removeCorner_preserves_containment","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L615-L615","doc":"Removing the row of a witnessed skew cell preserves\ncontainment. (Scoped to the witnessed cell's row: the earlier\nform quantified over an arbitrary `row`, which is false when\n`lam.part row = μ.part row`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.skewCorners_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.skewCorners_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L609-L609","doc":"A strict size increase yields a non-empty corner set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.cells_card_eq_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.cells_card_eq_size","kind":"theorem","line":607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L607-L607","doc":"`lam.cells.card = lam.size`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers.mk","kind":"ctor","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L605-L605","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.PartitionHelpers","kind":"class","line":602,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L602-L617","doc":"**Partition combinatorics — typeclass.** Bundles three\npartition / Young-diagram helpers; every field is backed by a\nproved theorem in this file (see `partitionHelpers_default`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_preserves_containment_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_preserves_containment_proved","kind":"theorem","line":539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L539-L592","doc":"**Removing the witnessed row preserves containment — proved.**\nIf `c ∈ lam/μ`, then decrementing `lam` at `c.row` (and\nre-sorting) still contains `μ`: at `c.row` we have\n`μ.part c.row ≤ c.col < lam.part c.row`, so the decremented\nentry still dominates `μ.part c.row`, and re-sorting preserves\npointwise domination of the antitone `μ.part`\n(`part_le_insertionSort_getD`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners_nonempty_proved","kind":"theorem","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L498-L537","doc":"**Skew-corner non-emptiness — proved.** The lexicographically\nmaximal cell of `lam/μ` (maximal row, then maximal column within\nthat row) is a skew corner: the cell below has a strictly larger\nrow and the cell to the right a strictly larger column in the\nmaximal row, so neither lies in `lam/μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_nonempty_of_size_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells_nonempty_of_size_lt","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L486-L496","doc":"A strict size increase gives a non-empty skew diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_subset_of_contains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_subset_of_contains","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L470-L484","doc":"Containment of partitions gives containment of Young-diagram\ncell sets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.part_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.part_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L373-L388","doc":"The parts of a partition are antitone (weakly decreasing),\nextended by `0` beyond the last part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.cells_card_eq_size_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.cells_card_eq_size_proved","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L348-L363","doc":"**Partition cells-count = size** — proved theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L314-L316","doc":"SYT count is nonneg (it's a natural number). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount_empty","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L308-L312","doc":"SYT count of empty skew shape is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSYTCount","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L281-L306","doc":"The number of skew SYT of shape lam/μ.\nDenoted f^{lam/μ} in the literature.\n\nDefined recursively: for each removable corner cell c of lam/μ,\nf^{lam/μ} = Σ_{c ∈ corners} f^{(lam \\ c)/μ}.\n\nBase case: f^{∅} = 1 (empty skew shape).\n\nTermination: lam.size - μ.size strictly decreases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_decreases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_decreases","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L272-L279","doc":"The termination measure for skewSYTCount decreases when\nremoving a corner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_size","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L264-L270","doc":"Removing a corner decreases the partition size by exactly 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.sum_insertionSort_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.sum_insertionSort_eq","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L255-L262","doc":"Sorting a list (by any relation) preserves its sum. Backed by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.sum_insertionSort_eq` (a candidate Mathlib\nupstream lemma); this alias preserves the local name used by\n`removeCorner_size`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.removeCorner_sum","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L214-L253","doc":"The sum of parts after removing a corner at row `row` equals\nthe original sum minus 1.\n\nProof: mapIdx changes exactly one element (at index `row`)\nfrom `p` to `p - 1`, reducing the sum by 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.removeCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.removeCorner","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L199-L212","doc":"Remove a corner cell from a partition.\nDecrements the part at the given row by 1, then re-sorts the\nlist to preserve the weakly-decreasing invariant.\n\nSorting after decrement is benign: when `row` *is* a corner,\nthe result is already sorted (the sort is the identity); when\n`row` is *not* a corner, sorting moves the decremented entry\nto the right place. The size (sum of parts) is invariant under\npermutation, so size-decrease lemmas continue to hold without\na corner hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCorners","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L193-L197","doc":"The corner cells of a skew shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.isSkewCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.isSkewCorner","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L185-L191","doc":"A corner cell of a skew shape lam/μ is a cell (i, j) ∈ lam/μ such that\n(i, j+1) ∉ lam/μ and (i+1, j) ∉ lam/μ.\nRemoving a corner from lam gives a valid partition with size one less. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.col_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.col_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L180-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.row_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.row_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L176-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT.mk","kind":"ctor","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L175-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.IsSkewSYT","kind":"structure","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L171-L183","doc":"A filling is a valid skew SYT if:\n1. It's a bijection from skew cells to {1, ..., |lam/μ|}\n2. Rows are strictly increasing (left to right)\n3. Columns are strictly increasing (top to bottom) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SkewFilling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.SkewFilling","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L168-L169","doc":"A filling of a skew diagram: assigns a natural number to each cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.mem_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.mem_cells","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L156-L164","doc":"Cell membership: (i,j) ∈ lam.cells ↔ i < lam.length ∧ j < lam.part i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.cells_empty","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L152-L154","doc":"The cells of the empty partition form the empty set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewSize","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L148-L150","doc":"The number of cells in a skew diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.skewCells","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L144-L146","doc":"The skew diagram lam/μ: cells in lam but not in μ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableContains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableContains","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L117-L140","doc":"Containment is decidable for finite partitions.\nWe check μ.part i ≤ lam.part i for all i up to max length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instLEPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instLEPartition","kind":"instance","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L114-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.contains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.contains","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L109-L112","doc":"Containment: μ ⊆ lam iff every part of μ is ≤ the corresponding\npart of lam. This is the partial order on the Young lattice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.cells","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L102-L107","doc":"The set of cells in a partition's Young diagram:\n{(i, j) : i < lam.length ∧ j < lam.part i}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.toProd_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.toProd_injective","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L91-L98","doc":"`toProd` is injective: two cells with the same row and col are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.toProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.toProd","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L88-L89","doc":"Embedding `Cell → ℕ × ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprCell","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprCell.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprCell.repr","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableEqCell.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableEqCell.decEq","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableEqCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instDecidableEqCell","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.col","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.row","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Cell","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L80-L84","doc":"A cell in a Young diagram: row i, column j. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.part","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The i-th part of a partition (0 if i ≥ length). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.length","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The length (number of parts) of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.size","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The size (weight) of a partition: sum of parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprPartition","kind":"instance","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprPartition.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.instReprPartition.repr","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.sorted","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SkewSYT.Partition","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SkewSYT.lean#L39-L45","doc":"A partition is a weakly decreasing list of positive naturals.\nWe represent it as `List ℕ` with the convention that trailing\nzeros are ignored (a partition of n has parts summing to n). ","signatureChunk":0}]}